[] I am under the impression that you engrave it on the floor, where you are
[] standing...how long does this take(turns)? What benifits does it give you?

Engraving Elbereth and Hand of Elbereth are unrelated except in their
reference to Elbereth.

Hand of Elbereth is a gift from the gods that grants you various
intrinsics. Also, if things are right you'll get a named weapon.

Engraving Elbereth is something you can do anytime. As long as the
engraving is unsmudged (look at it with ":") most monsters will not
attack you. However, attacking a monster usually has the effect of
smudging the engraving, again, under most circumstances. Engraving
is different depending on whether you use a bladed weapon, an athame,
a wand or other such things. Also, you could avoid smudging the
engraving by not standing on it but by standing _over_ it.

